From: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] networkmanager: match DHCP links by type, not by eth* name

The legacy "dhcp" network type wrote [Match] Name=e*. Photon boots with
net.ifnames=0, so the names are kernel-enumerated (eth0), and
systemd-networkd warns at every boot:

  eth0: Found matching .network file, based on potentially unpredictable
  interface name: /etc/systemd/network/50-dhcp-en.network

Match Type=ether with Kind=!* instead, the upstream systemd pattern for
all physical Ethernet links (virtual links such as veth have a kind).
The writer learns the "type" and "kind" match keys.

Signed-off-by: Daniel Casota <dcasota@gmail.com>
---
--- a/photon_installer/networkmanager.py	2026-01-21 23:43:56.000000000 +0100
+++ b/photon_installer/networkmanager.py	2026-09-26 10:13:38.234166446 +0200
@@ -147,7 +147,10 @@
         type = old_config['type']
         if type == 'dhcp':
             config['ethernets'] = {
-                'dhcp-en': {'match': {'name': 'e*'}, 'dhcp4': True}
+                # all physical Ethernet links; Kind=!* excludes virtual ones (veth,
+                # macvlan, ...). Unlike Name=e* this does not rely on the kernel-assigned
+                # eth* names that net.ifnames=0 produces, which networkd warns about.
+                'dhcp-en': {'match': {'type': 'ether', 'kind': '!*'}, 'dhcp4': True}
             }
         elif type == 'static':
             config['ethernets'] = {'static-en': {'match': {'name': 'eth0'}}}
@@ -249,6 +252,10 @@
                 if 'name' in iface_config['match']:
                     name = iface_config['match']['name']
                     sysdict['Match']['Name'] = name
+                if 'type' in iface_config['match']:
+                    sysdict['Match']['Type'] = iface_config['match']['type']
+                if 'kind' in iface_config['match']:
+                    sysdict['Match']['Kind'] = iface_config['match']['kind']
 
         else:
             raise Exception(f"unknown interface type {type}")
